      {
        "title": "Show HN: Things to Do API",
        "link": "https://thingstodoapi.com/",
        "description": "<p>I built an api/mcp for local events: pop-ups, one-off events, concerts, etc. currently covering the SF bay area.<p>I've been building a bunch of consumer apps lately around personalization and recommendation and have had a hard time finding this data in one spot. agents can find useful stuff through tool calls / web search, but slow.<p>you can scrape on demand too, but i wanted a faster data set and couldn't find an existing provider for the mix of event types I was searching for.<p>the methodology for it is to find influential accounts/posters/etc. and do a fan out across things that they co-post with.<p>mcp: `claude mcp add --transport http thingstodo <a href=\"https://api.thingstodoapi.com/mcp\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://api.thingstodoapi.com/mcp</a>`<p>I'm considering adding other cities. If you're building something that needs local event data, would something like this be useful and where would you want coverage?</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50126384\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50126384</a></p>\n<p>Points: 23</p>\n<p># Comments: 3</p>",
